Subject: [PATCH] app_server: fall back to any Noto Sans CJK variant

Missing glyphs fall back to a fixed list of Noto families, and the only CJK
entry was "Noto Sans CJK JP". On arm64 that family cannot be used: the
HaikuPorts package ships it as a variable font, which the arm64 freetype
(2.6.3) cannot load, so RENKU installs the static Noto Sans CJK KR faces
instead - and with nothing named JP installed, every Korean, Japanese and
Chinese string drew as boxes, even with a CJK font present.

All Noto Sans CJK variants carry the same Hangul, kana and Han glyph set;
list KR, SC and TC after JP so whichever is installed is used.

Found with haiku-korean-pack on arm64: the Korean catalogs loaded (menu and
column labels changed length) but rendered as empty boxes.

diff --git a/src/servers/app/font/GlyphLayoutEngine.h b/src/servers/app/font/GlyphLayoutEngine.h
index 85ecf015be..1a59419d84 100644
--- a/src/servers/app/font/GlyphLayoutEngine.h
+++ b/src/servers/app/font/GlyphLayoutEngine.h
@@ -419,6 +419,13 @@ GlyphLayoutEngine::PopulateFallbacks(
 		"Noto Sans",
 		"Noto Sans Thai",
 		"Noto Sans CJK JP",
+		// All Noto Sans CJK variants carry the same Hangul, kana and Han
+		// glyphs. Where the JP one cannot be had -- HaikuPorts ships it as a
+		// variable font, which an older freetype cannot load, so RENKU arm64
+		// installs the static KR faces instead -- any of the others will do.
+		"Noto Sans CJK KR",
+		"Noto Sans CJK SC",
+		"Noto Sans CJK TC",
 		"Noto Sans Cherokee",
 		"Noto Sans Symbols",
 		"Noto Sans Symbols 2",
